legacy line clamping: display:-webkit-box/-webkit-inline-box with a vertical -webkit-box-orient and a -webkit-line-clamp
is a flow-root/inline-block whose formatting context shows its first N lines: the box ends at line N and that line's
ending text run ends in an ellipsis when a line follows it. Without the clamp, a legacy box is a flex container along
its orient. CSS Overflow 4: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-overflow-4/#webkit-line-clamp

